          - APIRouter

===== .forge/ast-grep/rules/python/fastapi/no-raw-request-body.yml
# Generated by forge from python/fastapi/no-raw-request-body (mode: advise).
id: python/fastapi/no-raw-request-body
language: Python
severity: warning
message: "forge:python/fastapi/no-raw-request-body Advice: a route reads its input from a declared parameter (a Pydantic model body, Form(), File()), not from request.json(), .form(), .body() or .stream() on the Starlette Request, which skip validation and the OpenAPI schema. Reading the raw body stays right where the bytes matter, such as a webhook signature check."
rule:
  any:
    - pattern: await $REQ.json()
    - pattern: await $REQ.form($$$)
    - pattern: await $REQ.body()
    - pattern: $REQ.stream()
metadata:
  forge_where:
    REQ:
      type:
        package: starlette
        name: Request

===== .forge/ast-grep/rules/python/fastapi/no-testclient-in-async-test.yml
# Generated by forge from python/fastapi/no-testclient-in-async-test (mode: forbid).
id: python/fastapi/no-testclient-in-async-test
language: Python
severity: error
message: 'forge:python/fastapi/no-testclient-in-async-test No TestClient inside an async def: it runs the app on another event loop in a thread, so async fixtures (database sessions, pools) cross loops and fail or hang. Use httpx.AsyncClient(transport=httpx.ASGITransport(app=app), base_url="http://test").'
rule:
  kind: call
  pattern: $C
  inside:
    kind: function_definition
    regex: ^async[[:space:]]
    stopBy: end
metadata:
  forge_where:
    C:
      type:
        package: starlette
        name: TestClient

===== .forge/ast-grep/rules/python/fastapi/testclient-lifespan.yml
# Generated by forge from python/fastapi/testclient-lifespan (mode: advise).
id: python/fastapi/testclient-lifespan
language: Python
severity: warning
message: "forge:python/fastapi/testclient-lifespan Advice: TestClient(app) is entered as a context manager (with TestClient(app) as client:, a fixture yielding inside the with): otherwise the app's lifespan never runs, and startup work such as opening the database pool is skipped."
rule:
  kind: call
  pattern: $C
  not:
    inside:
      kind: with_item
      stopBy: end
metadata:
  forge_where:
    C:
      type:
        package: starlette
        name: TestClient

===== .forge/ast-grep/rules/python/llm-client-timeout.yml
# Generated by forge from python/llm-client-timeout (mode: forbid).
id: python/llm-client-timeout
language: Python
severity: error
message: "forge:python/llm-client-timeout Anthropic and OpenAI SDK clients and calls never set timeout=None (the client constructor, with_options(), a request): a request could then wait forever, and is retried. Keep the SDK's default or pass a number of seconds. requests and httpx are python/http-timeout."
rule:
